 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$3111K**.\n\nHow I got there:\n\n1. **Messages that don't count.** Only Finance Office budget entries were used. Notes from Engineering, PMO, Vendor, Sales and other teams were ignored. So were Finance Office entries about audits, reminders, invoices and cost centres.\n2. **Starting point.** #0001 set the budget to $1880K, and no later entry resets it.\n3. **Withdrawals.** Each withdrawal chain was resolved from the end. For example:\n   - #0632 \u2192 #0439 \u2192 #0112 \u2192 #0078 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0003 \u2192 #0002: #0632 withdraws #0439, which revives #0112. #0112 withdraws #0078, which revives #0007, which withdraws #0003. So #0003 does not stand, and the \u2212$36K in #0002 still applies.\n   - #1546 \u2192 #1403 \u2192 #1213 \u2192 #1203: #1213 stands, so the +$521K in #1203 is cancelled.\n   - #1424 \u2192 #1097 \u2192 #1091: #1097 is withdrawn, so the \u2212$4K in #1091 still applies.\n   - #1524 withdraws #1295, so that \u2212$12K is cancelled.\n4. **Running total.** I then applied every update that still stands, in order, from $1880K. The early steps are:\n   - #0002: \u2212$36K gives $1844K.\n   - #0006: \u2212$562K gives $1282K.\n   - #0014: +$556K gives $1838K.\n   - The total continues through the remaining updates, ending with #1597 (+$75K) and #1598 (+$5K).\n\nThis was done by hand across about 1,600 records, so a small slip is possible. I re-checked the withdrawal chains but did not recompute the full running total a second time.\n\nANSWER: $3111K",
